  "notes": "Jerk-adjacent abrasive alt-rap with a dark-plugg edge — heavy autotune, ear-piercing synths, distorted bass. Jerked snare clusters over a distorted bass carpet and lo-fi crushed hats; the melody is texture-first, a piercing high-register line over drones. ⚠ Confidence MEDIUM: the research draws on Music Fandom, MusicBrainz and 1c34 references rather than an interview, so the drums are the well-attested half and the harmony is the archetype's. ⛔ **129 distinct harmonies in 1000 seeds — by far the worst in the batch, and the fix is deliberately NOT more chords.** The research says the harmony is thin and lo-fi, 1-2 chords, and that is kept: what widened is how LONG a chord is held (2-16 beats, so a stab and a drone are both in range), the harmonic rhythm, and the voicing window. A model can be harmonically static without writing the same eight bars for every eighth seed — those are different claims, and only the second one is a defect. ⚠ The widest voicing window in the batch (46-84), which is what the research asks for anyway — *piercing high-register synth lines over drones* — plus a fourth two-chord family. Both were needed: this model measured 129 distinct harmonies in 1000 seeds on the first cut and the duration and rhythm widening only reached 404 of the required 500. ⛔ It stays a 1-2 chord model, which is what the research claims; what changed is how many different ways those chords can be voiced and ordered. ⚠  rebalanced from 0.80 triad to 0.50/0.34/0.16 — the research says *dissonance tolerated*, and a four-fifths-triad chord block was the least characterful thing in the model as well as the last thing holding its harmony count down. ⚠ And a sus substitution at 0.22, which took it over the 500 floor. A suspended voicing over a drone is the vowel-pad sound this lane actually makes, and it adds a chord QUALITY without adding a progression the research does not claim.",
